          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Home backup with a battery works when it is planned around loads rather than capacity. Write the critical-load list, find the largest starting surge, decide how the battery reaches hardwired circuits, and only then pick the unit. For most houses that means a 4kWh, expandable 120/240V system on a transfer switch; for overnight plug-in backup, a 2kWh unit is enough.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If your outages run for days, plan the recharge as carefully as the battery: solar on clear days, a small generator outdoors when skies are gray, and storage you can add before you need it.
